{
  "contract": "contracts/device-v1.md",
  "about": "Test vectors for device-v1 Part A, written by packages/mail-crypto (npm run write-device-vectors -w @proprietor/mail-crypto) and checked by its test/device-vectors.test.ts. Every key and secret is SHA-256 of the public label next to it: test values only, never used for real mail. Mailbox keys are clamped X25519 scalars; P-256 scalars d are SHA-256 of their label read as a big-endian integer. Byte strings are lowercase hex, except the stored forms (sealed, tag, signature, nonce, keyEnvelope, wrapped, descriptor) and the recipients' keys in tags, which are base64url without padding (RFC 4648 §5). The challenges and the device proof were made by a sealer and a signer written from the contract; Mail's are src/proofs.ts. Round 3: the factor and key challenges carry their action descriptor (contracts/action-descriptor-v1.md, as Mail issues it), the request it digests and its digest, and their associated data ends with that digest (A6). Each factor's `signing` holds ikmS, the candidate counter, sS and vS (A2b). `statements` holds one of each A11 statement (keys base64url) with its message, its signatures (the signer's public point in hex) and, under `changed`, values that each refuse every signature when they replace that one field. `graph` is the factor graph those statements make.",
